		{"id":"bf73e9cc29402134","type":"text","x":3300,"y":0,"width":350,"height":270,"text":"**● HUMAN** · book + web\n\n### [[People/Chris Maddison|Chris Maddison]]\n\nHinton MSc alumnus; Oxford DPhil with Doucet and Teh.\n\n[Profile / source](https://www.cs.toronto.edu/~cmaddis/maddison_cv.pdf)","color":"#43A8D1"},
		{"id":"538ecd9c4464b249","type":"text","x":3710,"y":0,"width":350,"height":270,"text":"**● HUMAN** · book + web\n\n### [[People/Alex Krizhevsky|Alex Krizhevsky]]\n\nToronto MSc alumnus and AlexNet coauthor.\n\n[Profile / source](https://cave.cs.toronto.edu/kriz/)","color":"#43A8D1"},
		{"id":"6d369be53901f462","type":"text","x":3300,"y":330,"width":350,"height":270,"text":"**● HUMAN** · book + web\n\n### [[People/Yann LeCun|Yann LeCun]]\n\nHinton postdoctoral alumnus; NYU professor and AMI Labs executive chairman in September 2026.\n\n[Profile / source](https://cims.nyu.edu/ai/events/919/)","color":"#43A8D1"},
		{"id":"661980806ee7a3fc","type":"text","x":3710,"y":330,"width":350,"height":270,"text":"**● HUMAN** · book + web\n\n### [[People/Peter Dayan|Peter Dayan]]\n\nComputational neuroscientist; former Gatsby director.\n\n[Profile / source](https://www.kyb.tuebingen.mpg.de/person/95844)","color":"#43A8D1"},
		{"id":"e42a2123a055cffc","type":"text","x":3300,"y":660,"width":350,"height":270,"text":"**● HUMAN** · book\n\n### [[People/Zoubin Ghahramani|Zoubin Ghahramani]]\n\nGoogle DeepMind scientist and interviewee.\n\n[[Sources/Hassabis - source book.pdf#page=465|PDF p. 465]] · profile pending","color":"#43A8D1"},
		{"id":"4eacd1bebb51c591","type":"text","x":3710,"y":660,"width":350,"height":270,"text":"**● HUMAN** · web extension\n\n### [[People/Alex Graves|Alex Graves]]\n\nIncluded because a sourced relationship names this entity.\n\nSee linked evidence note","color":"#43A8D1"},
		{"id":"25b3e949b8a0687d","type":"text","x":3300,"y":990,"width":350,"height":270,"text":"**● HUMAN** · web extension\n\n### [[People/Max Welling|Max Welling]]\n\nIncluded because a sourced relationship names this entity.\n\nSee linked evidence note","color":"#43A8D1"},
		{"id":"943d92411e915768","type":"text","x":4600,"y":0,"width":350,"height":270,"text":"**▣ LAB** · book + web\n\n### [[Labs/Gatsby Computational Neuroscience Unit|Gatsby Computational Neuroscience Unit]]\n\nUCL academic research unit; established 1998.\n\n[Profile / source](https://www.ucl.ac.uk/life-sciences/gatsby/about)","color":"#63BFA7"},
		{"id":"28437eb36c0500d4","type":"text","x":5010,"y":0,"width":350,"height":270,"text":"**■ COMPANY** · web extension\n\n### [[Companies/DNNresearch|DNNresearch]]\n\nToronto neural-network startup co-founded in 2012; acquired by Google 2013.\n\n[Profile / source](https://www.cs.utoronto.ca/~hinton/fullcv14.pdf)","color":"#E8AD59"},
		{"id":"5b2bd3707e895a1a","type":"text","x":4600,"y":330,"width":350,"height":270,"text":"**■ COMPANY** · book + web\n\n### [[Companies/Google|Google]]\n\nTechnology company; acquired DeepMind in 2014.\n\n[Profile / source](https://about.google/)","color":"#E8AD59"},
		{"id":"b36d0cbe95a8db86","type":"text","x":5010,"y":330,"width":350,"height":270,"text":"**■ COMPANY** · book + web\n\n### [[Companies/OpenAI|OpenAI]]\n\nAI research organization founded in 2015; this link documents its founding structure.\n\n[Profile / source](https://openai.com/index/introducing-openai/)","color":"#E8AD59"},
		{"id":"47accc116d7db4c5","type":"text","x":4600,"y":660,"width":350,"height":270,"text":"**■ COMPANY** · web extension\n\n### [[Companies/Safe Superintelligence|Safe Superintelligence]]\n\nAI research company; official updates establish Sutskever's CEO role.\n\n[Profile / source](https://ssi.inc/updates)","color":"#E8AD59"},
		{"id":"c996a33de3cb46d8","type":"text","x":5010,"y":660,"width":350,"height":270,"text":"**▣ LAB** · book + web\n\n### [[Labs/FAIR|FAIR]]\n\nIndustrial AI research unit; founding director LeCun.\n\n[Profile / source](https://cims.nyu.edu/ai/events/919/)","color":"#63BFA7"},
		{"id":"e4584bc9ad78e46e","type":"text","x":4600,"y":990,"width":350,"height":270,"text":"**◆ INSTITUTION** · book + web\n\n### [[Institutions/New York University|New York University]]\n\nUniversity; LeCun faculty affiliation.\n\n[Profile / source](https://www.nyu.edu/)","color":"#B19CDE"},
		{"id":"7ad7a086d09b63ce","type":"text","x":5010,"y":990,"width":350,"height":270,"text":"**■ COMPANY** · web extension\n\n### [[Companies/AMI Labs|AMI Labs]]\n\nCompany; NYU source identifies LeCun as executive chairman in 2026.\n\n[Profile / source](https://cims.nyu.edu/ai/events/919/)","color":"#E8AD59"},
		{"id":"bae71e892d50db7b","type":"text","x":1250,"y":1000,"width":650,"height":300,"text":"## Read supervision precisely\n\nLeCun and Dayan: **postdocs**.\n\nMaddison: Hinton **MSc**, then Oxford DPhil with Teh and Doucet.\n\nKrizhevsky: confirmed **MSc**; no completed PhD asserted.\n\nSee the linked notes for source disagreements and [Hinton’s full official PhD roster](https://www.cs.toronto.edu/~hinton/gradstuphd.html)."}
